      "title": "Implement Core Data Structures for Crystal Representation",
      "description": "Create the fundamental data models for representing crystal structures, including unit cells, atomic positions, and symmetry operations.",
      "status": "pending",
      "dependencies": [],
      "priority": "high",
      "details": "Develop Python classes for CrystalStructure, SymmetryOperation, and AnalysisResult as specified in the PRD. The CrystalStructure class should store unit cell parameters (a, b, c, alpha, beta, gamma), atomic positions, and metadata. The SymmetryOperation class should represent rotation, translation, and other symmetry transforms with appropriate matrix operations. Use NumPy arrays for efficient numerical operations. Ensure proper encapsulation and validation of input data.",
      "testStrategy": "Create unit tests for each class, verifying proper initialization, data validation, and basic operations. Test with known crystal structures from literature to ensure correct representation."
    },
